spec:
  grid: 20-27 rows x 21-27 cols, background=0
  frames:
    count: 3-5 hollow red(2) square frames, all same size within an example
    size: 5 or 7 (odd), yielding 3x3 or 5x5 interior
    interior: exactly one non-bg color per frame, all distinct; fill 30-56% of interior cells
    mask_pattern: arbitrary, 8-connected, at least 3 filled cells
    separation: frame bboxes never overlap; min gap >= 1 cell
  connectors:
    count: same as frame count (one per cycle edge)
    color: blue(1), each is a simple 4-connected path (no branching)
    turns: 0-2 direction changes; length 2-24 cells
    attachment: each endpoint touches exactly 1 cell of a frame border (single-cell contact)
    topology: forms a single Hamiltonian cycle over all frames (each frame has degree 2)
  cycle_order: frames sorted clockwise by center angle around their shared centroid
  transform:
    rule: recolor each frame's interior mask with the color from the next frame clockwise
    invariant: mask shapes, frame borders, connectors, and background unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (output trivially derived from input by color rotation)
  steps:
    1. Choose n_frames (3-5) and frame_size (5 or 7).
    2. Place n_frames non-overlapping square frames on a sufficiently large grid, arranged roughly in a cycle (ensure distinct clockwise angles from centroid).
    3. Generate a random 8-connected mask for each frame interior (fill 30-56%).
    4. Assign n distinct non-red/blue/bg colors, one per frame.
    5. Connect adjacent frames in the cycle with L-shaped blue paths (1-2 turns), attaching at one cell on each frame's border. Ensure connectors don't overlap frames or each other.
    6. Verify the clockwise ordering of frames matches the cycle edge adjacency.
    7. Output = rotate interior colors one step clockwise; input is the constructed grid.
